{"audio": "romans-03.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 189467, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1600, "text": "Romans, Chapter Three."}, {"start_ms": 1600, "end_ms": 4267, "text": "What advantage then hath the Jew?"}, {"start_ms": 4267, "end_ms": 6533, "text": "or what profit is there of circumcision?"}, {"start_ms": 6533, "end_ms": 11467, "text": "Much every way: chiefly, because that unto them were committed the oracles of God."}, {"start_ms": 11467, "end_ms": 13867, "text": "For what if some did not believe?"}, {"start_ms": 13867, "end_ms": 17067, "text": "shall their unbelief make the faith of God without effect?"}, {"start_ms": 17067, "end_ms": 26933, "text": "God forbid: yea, let God be true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy sayings, and mightest overcome when thou art judged."}, {"start_ms": 26933, "end_ms": 31733, "text": "But if our unrighteousness commend the righteousness of God, what shall we say?"}, {"start_ms": 31733, "end_ms": 34267, "text": "Is God unrighteous who taketh vengeance?"}, {"start_ms": 34267, "end_ms": 38667, "text": "(I speak as a man) God forbid: for then how shall God judge the world?"}, {"start_ms": 38667, "end_ms": 45733, "text": "For if the truth of God hath more abounded through my lie unto his glory; why yet am I also judged as a sinner?"}, {"start_ms": 45733, "end_ms": 53067, "text": "And not rather, (as we be slanderously reported, and as some affirm that we say,) Let us do evil, that good may come?"}, {"start_ms": 53067, "end_ms": 54800, "text": "whose damnation is just."}, {"start_ms": 54800, "end_ms": 55600, "text": "What then?"}, {"start_ms": 55600, "end_ms": 56933, "text": "are we better than they?"}, {"start_ms": 56933, "end_ms": 71067, "text": "No, in no wise: for we have before proved both Jews and Gentiles, that they are all under sin; As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one: There is none that understandeth, there is none that seeketh after God."}, {"start_ms": 71067, "end_ms": 78133, "text": "They are all gone out of the way, they are together become unprofitable; there is none that doeth good, no, not one."}, {"start_ms": 78133, "end_ms": 95733, "text": "Their throat is an open sepulchre; with their tongues they have used deceit; the poison of asps is under their lips: Whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness: Their feet are swift to shed blood: Destruction and misery are in their ways: And the way of peace have they not known:"}, {"start_ms": 95733, "end_ms": 98133, "text": "There is no fear of God before their eyes."}, {"start_ms": 98133, "end_ms": 108533, "text": "Now we know that what things soever the law saith, it saith to them who are under the law: that every mouth may be stopped, and all the world may become guilty before God."}, {"start_ms": 108533, "end_ms": 115467, "text": "Therefore by the deeds of the law there shall no flesh be justified in his sight: for by the law is the knowledge of sin."}, {"start_ms": 115467, "end_ms": 134000, "text": "But now the righteousness of God without the law is manifested, being witnessed by the law and the prophets; Even the righteousness of God which is by faith of Jesus Christ unto all and upon all them that believe: for there is no difference: For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;"}, {"start_ms": 134000, "end_ms": 150533, "text": "Being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus: Whom God hath set forth to be a propitiation through faith in his blood, to declare his righteousness for the remission of sins that are past, through the forbearance of God; To declare, I say,"}, {"start_ms": 150533, "end_ms": 156667, "text": "at this time his righteousness: that he might be just, and the justifier of him which believeth in Jesus."}, {"start_ms": 156667, "end_ms": 158400, "text": "Where is boasting then?"}, {"start_ms": 158400, "end_ms": 159467, "text": "It is excluded."}, {"start_ms": 159467, "end_ms": 160400, "text": "By what law?"}, {"start_ms": 160400, "end_ms": 161067, "text": "of works?"}, {"start_ms": 161067, "end_ms": 163333, "text": "Nay: but by the law of faith."}, {"start_ms": 163333, "end_ms": 168400, "text": "Therefore we conclude that a man is justified by faith without the deeds of the law."}, {"start_ms": 168400, "end_ms": 170267, "text": "Is he the God of the Jews only?"}, {"start_ms": 170267, "end_ms": 172533, "text": "is he not also of the Gentiles?"}, {"start_ms": 172533, "end_ms": 182400, "text": "Yes, of the Gentiles also: Seeing it is one God, which shall justify the circumcision by faith, and uncircumcision through faith."}, {"start_ms": 182400, "end_ms": 186000, "text": "Do we then make void the law through faith?"}, {"start_ms": 186000, "end_ms": 189467, "text": "God forbid: yea, we establish the law."}], "words": [{"t": "Romans,", "s": 466, "e": 790, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 830, "e": 1154, "si": 0}, {"t": "Three.", "s": 1215, "e": 1478, "si": 0}, {"t": "What", "s": 2342, "e": 2482, "si": 1}, {"t": "advantage", "s": 2522, "e": 3044, "si": 1}, {"t": "then", "s": 3124, "e": 3325, "si": 1}, {"t": "hath", "s": 3405, "e": 3605, "si": 1}, {"t": "the", "s": 3645, "e": 3746, "si": 1}, {"t": "Jew?", "s": 3786, "e": 4046, "si": 1}, {"t": "or", "s": 4688, "e": 4768, "si": 2}, {"t": "what", "s": 4788, "e": 4929, "si": 2}, {"t": "profit", "s": 4989, "e": 5330, "si": 2}, {"t": "is", "s": 5370, "e": 5450, "si": 2}, {"t": "there", "s": 5490, "e": 5651, "si": 2}, {"t": "of", "s": 5651, "e": 5711, "si": 2}, {"t": "circumcision?", "s": 5771, "e": 6453, "si": 2}, {"t": "Much", "s": 6794, "e": 6974, "si": 3}, {"t": "every", "s": 7034, "e": 7235, "si": 3}, {"t": "way:", "s": 7315, "e": 7616, "si": 3}, {"t": "chiefly,", "s": 8037, "e": 8458, "si": 3}, {"t": "because", "s": 8539, "e": 8960, "si": 3}, {"t": "that", "s": 9160, "e": 9301, "si": 3}, {"t": "unto", "s": 9401, "e": 9602, "si": 3}, {"t": "them", "s": 9642, "e": 9802, "si": 3}, {"t": "were", "s": 98